# Windows PowerShell shell

The user shell is Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell`), not bash and not PowerShell 7. `&&` and `||` are parse errors here. This has failed repeatedly. Do not use them.

## How to run commands

- Put the working directory in the tool's working-directory field. Do not `cd` and then chain the real command.
- Run independent commands as separate shell calls.
- When one command must finish before the next in the same call, put each command on its own line, or separate them with `;` only when the later command should run even if the earlier one failed.
- When the next command must run only after success, check the result:

```powershell
python script.py
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
python other.py
```

## Do not write

```powershell
Set-Location hei_backend && python -m pytest
cd hei_frontend && npm test
git add . && git commit -m "msg"
```

## Write instead

```powershell
python -m pytest
```

with the working directory set to `hei_backend`, or:

```powershell
Set-Location hei_backend
python -m pytest
```

Do not suggest `&&` in instructions the user will paste into PowerShell.
